          String: ""
        DescriptionText:
          ClassType1: TEXT
          String: |-
            Aligns particle quads to face their render camera and,  optionally, orient and stretch along the particle's velocity vector. 
            
            Facing Mode and Alignment determines how the particle quads orients itself relative to the camera.
            
            Velocity Stretch Amount - controls how much the particle is scaled along the velocity vector.  When Stretch Amount is 0,  particles only face the camera and are oriented relative to the facing mode and alignment options.
            
            Pivot Point - an offset for both the center of the velocity stretch and rotations.  Setting Pivot Point to (0.0, -0.5) will make the stretch only happen behind the particle.
            
            Facing Mode: Camera Position - The particle quads normal toward the camera.
            Facing Mode: Camera Plane - The particle quads normal towards the closest point on the camera view plane.
            
            Alignment: World Up - The particle quads tangent towards the world's up.
            Alignment: Camera Up - The particle quads tangent towards the camera's up facing direction vector.
        Locked:
          Variable: false
        SubGraphUniqueID110:
          Variable: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        SubGraphUniqueID112:
          ClassType2: PARTICLE
          IOType: 1
